CHAPTER I GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Special Act on Disaster Risk Reduction Projects and Relocation Measures and matters necessary for its enforcement.

CHAPTER II DESIGNATION OF DISASTER RISK REDUCTION PROJECT DISTRICTS

Article 2 (Members of Disaster Risk Reduction Project Deliberative Committees)
(1) "Public officials of central administrative agencies prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 3(2) of the Special Act on Disaster Risk Reduction Projects and Relocation Measures (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means public officials falling under any of the following subparagraphs: <Amended 2016.11.29, 2017.7.26, 2025.10.1>
1. General-service public officials belonging to the Senior Civil Service of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety;
2. Public officials recommended by the heads of the respective central administrative agencies from among general-service public officials belonging to the Senior Civil Service who are in charge of disaster prevention-related duties at the following central administrative agencies:
(a) The Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs;
(b) The Ministry of Climate, Energy and Environment;
(c) The Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport;
(d) Other central administrative agencies that the Minister of the Interior and Safety deems should be represented on the Central Disaster Risk Reduction Project Deliberative Committee under Article 3(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Central Deliberative Committee").
(2) "Public officials of local governments prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 3(3) of the Act means bureau director-level public officials in charge of disaster prevention-related duties who belong to a Special Metropolitan City, Metropolitan City, Special Self-Governing City, Do, or Special Self-Governing Province (hereinafter referred to as a "City/Do"). <Amended 2016.11.29>

Article 3 (Operation, etc. of Disaster Risk Reduction Project Deliberative Committees)
(1) The chairpersons of the Central Deliberative Committee and the Local Disaster Risk Reduction Project Deliberative Committee under Article 3(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Local Deliberative Committee") shall convene and preside over meetings of their respective committees. <Amended 2016.11.29>
(2) Meetings of the Central Deliberative Committee and the Local Deliberative Committee shall open with the attendance of a majority of the incumbent members and adopt resolutions by the affirmative vote of a majority of the members present.
(3) The Central Deliberative Committee and the Local Deliberative Committee shall each have a secretary as follows: <Amended 2014.11.19, 2016.11.29, 2017.7.26>
1. Central Deliberative Committee: A public official of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety designated by the Minister of the Interior and Safety;
2. Local Deliberative Committee: A public official of the City/Do designated by the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, Metropolitan City Mayor, Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Do Governor, or Special Self-Governing Province Governor (hereinafter referred to as the "Mayor/Do Governor").
(4) Deleted. <2016.11.29>

Article 4 (Attachments to Applications for Designation of Disaster Risk Reduction Project Districts)
The matters to be attached to an application for designation of a disaster risk reduction project district (hereinafter referred to as an "improvement project district") pursuant to Article 4(3)7 of the Act shall be as follows: <Amended 2008.12.31, 2009.8.18, 2012.7.20, 2013.3.23, 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>
1. A statement of the reasons why designation as an improvement project district is necessary;
2. A location map at a scale of 1:25,000;
3. Topographical drawings under Article 8(2) of the Framework Act on the Regulation of Land Use;
4. Photographs of current conditions;
5. Materials relating to the regional transport system around the area where a disaster risk reduction project (hereinafter referred to as an "improvement project") is planned (limited to improvement project districts with an area equal to or greater than the area prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety);
6. Materials for consultation on strategic environmental impact assessments and small-scale environmental impact assessments under Article 22(2)8 of the Act;
7. A flood trace map under Article 21(2) of the Countermeasures against Natural Disasters Act.

Article 5 (Requirements for Designation of Improvement Project Districts)
Where an improvement project district is designated pursuant to Article 5, subparagraph 4 of the Act, fundamental measures for disaster prevention shall be reflected in the disaster risk reduction project plan (hereinafter referred to as the "improvement project plan").

Article 6 (Minor Changes to Improvement Project Districts)
"Changes to minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso to Article 6(1) of the Act means a reduction of up to 10 percent in the area of an improvement project district.

Article 7 (Public Notice and Public Announcement, etc. of Improvement Project Districts)
(1) Where the Minister of the Interior and Safety, a Mayor/Do Governor, or the head of a Si, Gun, or autonomous Gu (hereinafter referred to as the "head of a Si/Gun") gives public notice and makes a public announcement of the designation of an improvement project district pursuant to Article 6(2) of the Act, the public notice and public announcement shall include the following matters: <Amended 2009.8.18, 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>
1. The name of the improvement project district;
2. The location of the improvement project district;
3. The area designated as the improvement project district;
4. The implementer of the improvement project;
5. Topographical drawings under Article 8(2) of the Framework Act on the Regulation of Land Use.
(2) Where public notice and public announcement are given of changes to a designated improvement project district, the matters referred to in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) shall be included, and the details before and after the change shall be publicly notified and publicly announced together.

Article 8 (Restrictions on Acts, etc.)
(1) The acts requiring permission from the head of a Si/Gun having jurisdiction pursuant to Article 7(1) of the Act shall be the following acts: <Amended 2021.1.5>
1. New construction, reconstruction, extension, rebuilding, relocation, or change in use of buildings, or installation of structures;
2. Alteration of the form and quality of land, extraction of earth, sand, or stone, or excavation (digging) or subdivision of land;
3. Cutting or planting trees;
4. Piling up objects (meaning piling up objects that are not readily movable for one month or longer).
(2) When granting permission under paragraph (1), the head of a Si/Gun having jurisdiction shall hear the opinions of the project implementer under Article 8 of the Act.
(3) The acts that may be performed within an improvement project district without permission from the head of a Si/Gun having jurisdiction pursuant to Article 7(2)2 of the Act shall be the following acts: <Amended 2008.12.31, 2013.3.23, 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>
1. Alteration of the form and quality of land for cultivation, or temporary planting of ornamental plants (excluding temporary planting on cultivated land);
2. Installation of simple structures prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety that are directly used for the production of agricultural or fishery products.
(4) Pursuant to Article 7(3) of the Act, a person who, at the time of designation and public notice of an improvement project district, has commenced construction or a project for an act for which permission has already been obtained or is not required under relevant statutes or regulations shall report to the head of a Si/Gun having jurisdiction within 30 days from the date on which the improvement project district is designated and publicly notified, accompanied by a statement of the progress of the construction or project and an implementation plan.

CHAPTER III IMPLEMENTATION OF DISASTER RISK REDUCTION PROJECTS

Article 9 (Establishment of Corporations, Designation of Project Agents, Selection of Construction Contractors, etc.)
(1) Deleted. <2009.8.18>
(2) A project implementer under Article 8(1) of the Act may have a business operator engaged in site preparation, housing construction, or the like perform the following parts of an improvement project on its behalf, as prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety: <Amended 2008.12.31, 2009.8.18, 2013.3.23, 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>
1. Implementation design;
2. Works for reducing disaster risk and preparing residential sites for relocation;
3. Infrastructure works;
4. Sale of improved and developed sites;
5. Construction and sale of buildings and housing.

Article 10 (Minor Changes to Improvement Project Plans)
Where an approved improvement project plan is amended pursuant to the proviso to Article 9(2) of the Act, changes to minor matters that do not require approval from the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Mayor/Do Governor mean any of the following changes: <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>
1. An increase or decrease in project costs within 10 percent of the disaster risk reduction project costs (hereinafter referred to as "improvement project costs");
2. A reduction in area within 10 percent of the area of the improvement project district;
3. An increase or decrease within 10 percent of the approved installation area of equipment and facilities;
4. A change in the address of the project implementer;
5. A change in the representative of a project implementer that is a corporation.

Article 11 (Matters to Be Included in Improvement Project Plans)
The matters to be included in an improvement project plan pursuant to Article 9(3)8 of the Act shall be as follows:
1. Improvement project costs and a funding plan (including annual fund investment plans and financing plans);
2. Drawings showing the improvement project plan on a topographical map or cadastral map at a scale of 1:5,000 or larger;
3. Matters concerning the application of district-level flood protection standards under Article 18 of the Countermeasures against Natural Disasters Act within the improvement project district (included only where recommended by the head of a Si/Gun);
4. The opinions of the head of a Si/Gun having jurisdiction on the implementation of the improvement project, and matters concerning whether the opinions of residents, etc. under Article 14 of the Act have been reflected.

Article 12 (Details concerning Formulation of Disaster Risk Reduction Project Implementation Plans)
(1) Where a project implementer formulates a disaster risk reduction project implementation plan pursuant to Article 10(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as an "implementation plan"), the implementation plan shall include the following matters: <Amended 2008.10.29, 2008.12.31, 2009.8.18, 2013.3.23, 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>
1. Improvement project costs and a funding plan (including annual fund input plans and financing plans);
2. A location map and a plan drawing of the improvement project site;
3. Construction design documents (schematic design documents in the case of a project requiring consultation on construction under Article 29 of the Building Act);
4. Deleted. <2009.8.18>
5. The locations, lot numbers, land categories, and areas of land, objects, etc. to be expropriated or used pursuant to Article 18(1) of the Act; particulars of ownership and rights other than ownership; and the names and addresses of their owners and right holders;
6. A plan for the phased implementation of the improvement project (limited to cases where phased implementation is necessary in light of the conditions of the project);
7. A plan for disposing of land, buildings, etc. developed through the improvement project;
8. Documents for consultation on matters for which determinations, authorizations, permissions, consultations, consents, licenses, approvals, dispositions, releases, orders, designations, etc. (hereinafter referred to as "authorizations, permissions, etc.") are sought to be deemed to have been obtained pursuant to Article 17(1) of the Act;
9. Other matters prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety.
(2) Where the Minister of the Interior and Safety or a Mayor/Do Governor gives public notice of an implementation plan pursuant to Article 10(3) of the Act, the public notice shall include the following matters: <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>
1. The name of the improvement project;
2. The name and address of the project implementer and the name of its representative;
3. The purpose and outline of the improvement project;
4. The implementation period of the improvement project;
5. The location and area of the improvement project site.

Article 13 (Minor Changes to Implementation Plans)
Where an approved implementation plan is changed pursuant to the proviso to Article 10(1) of the Act, the matters for which the project implementer need not obtain approval from the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Mayor/Do Governor shall be as follows. In such cases, the project implementer shall notify the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Mayor/Do Governor of the changes without delay. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>
1. An increase or decrease in project costs within a range of 10 percent of the improvement project costs;
2. A decrease in area within a range of 10 percent of the area of the improvement project district;
3. An increase or decrease within a range of 10 percent of the approved installation area of equipment and facilities;
4. A change in the address of the project implementer;
5. A change in the representative of a project implementer that is a corporation.

Article 14 (Matters for Consultation with Residents on Relocation Measures Plans, Etc.)
Where a project implementer consults with residents subject to relocation in order to establish a relocation measures plan pursuant to Article 11(2) of the Act, the matters for consultation shall include the following: <Amended on December 31, 2008; March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>
1. The name of the project for the relocation measures district;
2. The location of the relocation measures district;
3. The period for implementing the project for the relocation measures district;
4. The area designated as the relocation measures district;
5. The number of buildings to be relocated to the relocation measures district;
6. The area of the building site for each individual relocating to the relocation measures district;
7. Project costs for implementing the relocation measures;
8. Other matters prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety.

Article 15 (Completion Inspections)
Where a project implementer intends to undergo a completion inspection pursuant to Article 12(1) of the Act, the project implementer shall submit to the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Mayor/Do Governor an application for a completion inspection, accompanied by the following documents: <Amended on December 31, 2008; March 23, 2013; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>
1. A statement of completion (including as-built design documents and completion photographs);
2. A plan based on actual measurements and a plan showing area calculations, as recognized by the head of a Si/Gun;
3. A statement of land areas by use and a plan drawing;
4. Deleted. <December 12, 2017>
5. A statement of areas by owner within the improvement project district after completion of the improvement project;
6. A statement of owners of facilities within the improvement project district after completion of the improvement project;
7. Documents and drawings necessary for consultation with the heads of relevant administrative agencies for completion inspections concerning authorizations, permissions, etc. under Article 12(2) of the Act;
8. A statement and drawings showing the vesting of public facilities, etc. under Article 32 of the Act;
9. A comparative map of the old and new cadastres;
10. Matters concerning the results of implementing the district-level flood protection standards under Article 18 of the Countermeasures against Natural Disasters Act within the improvement project district (limited to cases recommended by the head of the Si/Gun with jurisdiction);
11. Regional safety diagnoses and trends in changes in safety ratings under Article 75-2 of the Countermeasures against Natural Disasters Act (to be submitted only where the project implementer is a local government);
12. Other documents prescribed by Ordinance of the Ministry of the Interior and Safety.

Article 16 (Public Announcement of Completion of Improvement Projects)
Where the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Mayor/Do Governor publicly announces the completion of construction pursuant to Article 13(1) of the Act, the announcement shall include the following matters: <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>
1. The name of the improvement project;
2. The name and address of the project implementer and the name of its representative;
3. The location of the site where the improvement project is implemented;
4. The area of the site where the improvement project is implemented and the area by use;
5. The date of completion;
6. Matters concerning the management and disposition of major facilities.

Article 17 (Hearing Opinions of Residents, Etc.)
(1) Where the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Mayor/Do Governor intends to hear the opinions of residents, etc. pursuant to Article 14 of the Act, the Minister or Mayor/Do Governor shall send copies of the relevant documents to the head of the Si/Gun with jurisdiction: Provided, That this shall not apply where minor matters are to be changed pursuant to Articles 6, 10, and 13, or where the head of the Si/Gun with jurisdiction has already heard the opinions of residents, etc. pursuant to Article 14 of the Act. <Amended on August 18, 2009; November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>
(2) Upon receipt of the relevant documents pursuant to paragraph (1), the head of the Si/Gun shall publicly announce the following matters in the official bulletin of the local government, etc., and make the documents available for inspection by residents for 14 days:
1. The scope of the proposed improvement project district;
2. An outline of the project, such as the name, location, and area of the implementation plan;
3. Other matters deemed necessary by the head of the Si/Gun.
(3) The project implementer shall hold a residents' briefing within 1 month after the expiry of the public announcement period under paragraph (2), and shall do so after publicly announcing the following matters for at least 10 days in a place easily accessible to residents, etc., such as bulletin boards at Si, Gun, or Gu offices:
1. The purpose of the residents' briefing and its scheduled date, time, and place;
2. An outline of the improvement project;
3. Matters concerning the presentation of opinions.
(4) Where the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Mayor/Do Governor deems it necessary, the Minister or Mayor/Do Governor may hold a public hearing to hear the opinions of residents, etc. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>
(5) Where a public hearing is held pursuant to paragraph (4), the following matters shall be publicly announced at least once, no later than 14 days before the scheduled date of the public hearing, through a daily newspaper whose main circulation area is the relevant Si/Do, the Official Gazette, an official bulletin, a website, or other means: <Amended on November 24, 2020>
1. The purpose of the public hearing and its scheduled date, time, and place;
2. An outline of the improvement project;
3. Matters concerning applications to present opinions.
(6) Residents, owners of land, etc., and other interested persons may submit written or oral opinions during the public announcement period or by attending a residents' briefing or public hearing.
(7) Where opinions are submitted during the public announcement period, the head of the Si/Gun shall compile them and submit them to the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Mayor/Do Governor. <Amended on November 19, 2014; July 26, 2017>

Chapter IV Measures and Support for the Implementation of Improvement Projects, Etc.

Article 18 (Volume of Issuance of Land Redemption Bonds)
The volume of issuance of bonds redeemable in land or buildings developed through the implementation of a project under Article 19(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "land redemption bonds") shall be such that the land to be provided in redemption of those land redemption bonds does not exceed 50 percent of the area of land to be developed and offered for sale under the relevant improvement project.

Article 19 (Institutions Guaranteeing Land Redemption Bonds)
Pursuant to the proviso to Article 19(1) of the Act, persons falling under Article 8(1)3 and 4 of the Act may issue land redemption bonds only where they have obtained a payment guarantee from a bank under Article 2(1)2 of the Banking Act (hereinafter referred to as a "bank") or an insurance company under subparagraph 6 of Article 2 of the Insurance Business Act. <Amended on August 18, 2009; November 15, 2010; January 24, 2011>

Article 20 (Plans for Issuance of Land Redemption Bonds)
A plan for issuance of land redemption bonds that a project implementer must prepare pursuant to Article 19(2) of the Act shall include the following matters:
1. The name of the land redemption bonds;
2. The name of the project implementer;
3. The total issue amount of the land redemption bonds;
4. The interest rate on the land redemption bonds;
5. The method of redemption of the land redemption bonds;
6. The area designated for redemption or the use of the land designated for redemption;
7. The method of estimating the prices of the relevant land;
8. The guaranteeing institution and the details of the guarantee.

Article 21 (Public Announcement of Issuance of Land Redemption Bonds)
Where a project implementer issues land redemption bonds, the project implementer shall publicly announce the name of the land redemption bonds and the matters specified in the subparagraphs of Article 20: Provided, That the public announcement may be omitted where these matters have been included in the compensation plan under Article 15 of the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land, etc. for Public Works Projects and publicly announced, or where individual notifications have been sent to the owners of land, etc.

Article 22 (Interest Rates on Land Redemption Bonds, Etc.)
(1) The interest rate on land redemption bonds shall be determined by the issuer of the land redemption bonds, taking into account bank deposit interest rates and real estate supply and demand conditions at the time of issuance. <Amended on November 15, 2010>
(2) Land redemption bonds shall take the form of registered securities.

Article 23 (Subscription for Land Redemption Bonds, Etc.)
A person intending to receive the proceeds from the sale of land, etc. in land redemption bonds (hereinafter referred to as a "subscriber") shall prepare 2 copies of a land redemption bond subscription application stating the following matters and submit them to the project implementer:
1. The name of the project;
2. The name (in the case of a corporation, its corporate name and the name of its representative) and address of the subscriber;
3. Details of the land, etc. owned by the subscriber;
4. The amount to be received in land redemption bonds;
5. The sale proceeds of land other than the land subject to the land redemption bonds.

Article 24 (Matters to Be Stated on Land Redemption Bonds)
Land redemption bonds shall state the following matters, and the issuer shall affix their name and seal:
1. The name of the project implementer;
2. The interest rate on the land redemption bonds;
3. The method of redemption of the land redemption bonds;
4. The area designated for redemption or the use of the land designated for redemption;
5. The method of estimating land prices;
6. The land redemption bond number;
7. The date of issuance of the land redemption bond.

Article 25 (Maintenance of a Land Redemption Bond Register)
The issuer of land redemption bonds shall maintain at its principal office a land redemption bond register stating the following matters:
1. The land redemption bond number;
2. The date of issuance of the land redemption bond;
3. The matters specified in subparagraphs 2 through 6 of Article 20;
4. The name and address of the owner of the land redemption bond;
5. The date on which the owner of the land, etc. acquired the land redemption bond.

Article 26 (Transfer of Land Redemption Bonds, Etc.)
(1) Where a land redemption bond is transferred, the transferee shall request the issuer to enter the transferee's name and address in the land redemption bond register, and unless the acquirer's name and address are entered in the land redemption bond register, the acquirer may not assert the transfer against the issuer or a third party.
(2) Where a land redemption bond is made subject to a pledge, the pledgee shall request that the pledgee's name and address be entered in the land redemption bond register, and unless the pledgee's name and address are entered in the land redemption bond register, the pledgee may not assert the pledge against the issuer or a third party.
(3) Where a pledge is created pursuant to paragraph (2), the issuer of the land redemption bond shall indicate that fact on the land redemption bond.
(4) Upon receipt of a request under paragraph (1) or (2), the issuer of the land redemption bond shall comply with the request.

Article 27 (Notices to Owners of Land Redemption Bonds)
A notice or demand to the owner of a land redemption bond shall be sent to the address entered in the land redemption bond register: Provided, That, where the owner of the land redemption bond has separately notified the issuer of the land redemption bond of an address, the notice or demand shall be sent to that address.

Article 28 (Advance Payments)
(1) A project implementer who intends to receive advance payments from persons seeking to be supplied with or to use land, buildings, structures, or other property developed through an improvement project pursuant to Article 20 of the Act shall satisfy all of the following requirements and obtain approval from the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Mayor/Do Governor. <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>
1. Approval of the implementation plan shall have been obtained;
2. Ownership of at least 50 percent of the land area of the improvement project district shall have been secured, and the improvement project shall have commenced;
3. Ownership of the land, buildings, or structures to be supplied shall have been secured, and mortgages established on that land shall have been cancelled;
4. The rate of construction progress of the improvement project on the land to be supplied shall be at least 10 percent;
5. Confirmation shall have been obtained from the competent head of Si/Gun that the establishment and relocation of business establishments are proceeding normally in accordance with the written agreement under Article 4 (2) of the Act;
6. To secure the refund of advance payments in the event of non-performance of the supply contract, guarantee documents, such as payment guarantees, securities, guarantee insurance policies, time deposit certificates, or beneficiary certificates under Article 37 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Act on Contracts to Which the State Is a Party (hereinafter referred to as "guarantee documents, etc."; the same shall apply in this Article), containing the matters specified in the following items shall be submitted to the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Mayor/Do Governor: Provided, That, in the case of item (b), where the project period is extended, guarantee documents, etc. providing for a guarantee or insurance period equal to the original guarantee or insurance period plus the period of the intended extension shall be submitted.
(a) The guarantee or insurance amount shall be at least the advance payment plus the amount equivalent to the agreed interest for the guarantee or insurance period;
(b) The guarantee or insurance period shall begin on or before the date of receipt of the advance payment and end after the scheduled completion date, with an interval of at least one month between the scheduled completion date and the end of the guarantee or insurance period.
(2) After a project implementer supplies land, buildings, or structures or allows their use in advance of the public announcement of completion of construction pursuant to paragraph (1), the project implementer shall not provide the land or other property as collateral.
(3) Where the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Mayor/Do Governor determines that a project implementer has failed to perform the supply contract or lacks the capacity to carry out the project due to bankruptcy or other circumstances concerning the project implementer (including court decisions and approvals under the Debtor Rehabilitation and Bankruptcy Act), the Minister or Mayor/Do Governor may use the guarantee documents, etc. to refund advance payments before completion of the relevant improvement project. <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>

Article 29 (Relationship to Other Acts)
(1) Pursuant to Article 22 (2) 1 of the Act, private housing within an improvement project district may be specially supplied to the following persons, notwithstanding Article 54 of the Housing Act. <Amended 2016.8.11>
1. Persons subject to relocation within the relevant improvement project district;
2. Persons falling under either of the following items who have obtained confirmation from the competent head of Si/Gun:
(a) Teachers or employees of educational institutions established in the relevant improvement project district;
(b) Employees of State agencies, local governments, government-invested institutions, or research institutes within the relevant improvement project district.
(2) Where a business plan for a sports facility business under the Installation and Utilization of Sports Facilities Act is amended pursuant to the proviso to Article 22 (2) 6 (a) of the Act, minor amendments to the business plan that do not require approval from the competent head of Si/Gun shall be as follows:
1. Matters concerning a change in the name or address of the representative where the person who has obtained approval of the business plan is a corporation (excluding succession to approval of a business plan under Article 27 (3) of the Installation and Utilization of Sports Facilities Act);
2. Matters concerning a change in the trade name;
3. Matters concerning the installation or alteration of facilities falling under either of the following items that do not change the area or boundaries of the site for which the business plan has been approved:
(a) In the case of essential facilities under Article 27 (2) of the Installation and Utilization of Sports Facilities Act: Extension, reconstruction, or alteration within 30 percent of the area of each facility for which the business plan has been approved or each registered facility (meaning the gross floor area in the case of a building);
(b) In the case of facilities other than the essential facilities under item (a): Extension, reconstruction, relocation, rebuilding, or alteration of facilities for which the business plan has been approved or registered facilities;
4. Matters concerning a change in the planned number of members to be recruited or membership admission fees;
5. Matters concerning a change in the scheduled commencement date or scheduled completion date of construction to install business facilities for a sports facility business subject to registration.
(3) Where a sports facility business is registered and its registered particulars are changed pursuant to the proviso to Article 22 (2) 6 (b) of the Act, minor changes to registered particulars for which registration of the change with the head of Si/Gun is not required shall be as follows:
1. Matters concerning a change in the operator of a sports facility business resulting from succession to the sports facility business under Article 27 of the Installation and Utilization of Sports Facilities Act;
2. Matters concerning renovation and repair within a scope that does not change the site area or scale of the business facilities of the registered sports facility business;
3. Matters concerning use for other purposes during a period of seasonal closure without alteration of the facilities of a ski resort business.

Article 30 (Scope of Infrastructure Installation)
The scope of installation by type of facility to be installed at the expense of a person other than the project implementer pursuant to Article 23 (2) of the Act shall be as follows. <Amended 2009.8.18, 2012.4.10, 2014.7.14, 2021.1.5>
1. Roads: Roads satisfying all of the following requirements:
(a) The road shall have been designated as an urban/Gun planning facility under the National Land Planning and Utilization Act or as a road zone under Article 25 of the Road Act before the designation of the improvement project district;
(b) The road shall be a national road, local road, or State-supported local road under the Road Act that a local government is required to install.
2. Water supply and sewerage facilities: Water supply and sewerage pipelines that pass through without being connected to water supply and sewerage pipelines within the improvement project district;
3. Electricity facilities: Electricity facilities extending from main facilities outside the improvement project district to the boundary of an individual parcel adjoining an urban/Gun planning road at least eight meters wide under the land use plan within the improvement project district (hereinafter referred to as an "individual parcel"): Provided, That where main electricity facilities within the improvement project district are installed as underground lines at the request of the project implementer, the electricity supplier and the person requesting underground installation shall each bear 50 percent of the installation costs;
4. Gas supply facilities: Gas supply facilities extending from main gas supply facilities outside the improvement project district to the boundary of an individual parcel: Provided, That where a constant-pressure control room (a room for maintaining and regulating constant pressure) is installed within an individual parcel in the improvement project district to supply gas for cooking or individual heating (excluding central heating), the costs to be borne shall be the costs of installing gas supply facilities up to that constant-pressure control room;
5. District heating facilities: Heat transmission pipes extending from the branch point of the main heat transmission pipes serving the improvement project district to the shut-off valve at the entrance to each mechanical equipment room of an individual parcel in the improvement project district;
6. Telecommunications facilities: Conduit facilities extending from main facilities outside the improvement project district to the boundary of an individual parcel in the improvement project district, and cable facilities extending from main facilities outside the improvement project district to the first terminal within an individual parcel in the improvement project district.

Article 31 (Conditions for Payment of the Sale Price of State or Public Property)
Where the State or a local government sells State property or public property to a project implementer pursuant to Article 24 (4) of the Act, payment of the price may be allowed in equal annual installments over a period not exceeding 20 years. In such cases, the interest applicable during the installment payment period shall be determined at a rate between 3 percent and 6 percent.

Article 32 (Repurchase Price)
Where the owner of land or other property at the time of expropriation, or the owner's universal successor, repurchases land or other property that is no longer necessary for an improvement project pursuant to Article 25 (1) of the Act, the owner or universal successor shall pay the project implementer the compensation amount plus statutory interest from the date on which compensation was paid to the date of repurchase.

CHAPTER V SUPPLEMENTARY PROVISIONS

Article 33 (Service of Documents by Public Notice)
(1) Where a project implementer effects service by public notice pursuant to Article 27 (2) of the Act, the project implementer shall publicly announce the contents of the documents to be served at least once in a daily newspaper with nationwide circulation as its principal circulation area and a daily newspaper whose principal circulation area is the relevant improvement project district (hereinafter referred to as "daily newspapers"; the same shall apply in this Article).
(2) Where service is effected by public notice pursuant to paragraph (1), the documents shall be deemed to have reached the other party when 14 days have elapsed from the date on which they were publicly announced in the daily newspapers.

Article 34 (Public Notice of Dispositions for Supervision and Project Management)
Where the Minister of the Interior and Safety or the Mayor/Do Governor makes a disposition under Article 29 (1) of the Act, the Minister or Mayor/Do Governor shall publicly notify the following matters without delay. <Amended 2014.11.19, 2017.7.26>
1. The name of the improvement project plan or improvement project;
2. The name and address of the project implementer and the name of its representative;
3. The location and area of the land subject to the improvement project or the improvement project district;
4. The details of and reasons for the disposition.

Article 35 (Vesting of Public Facilities, etc.)
(1) "Facilities prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 32 (1) of the Act means the following facilities. <Amended 2008.5.26>
1. Communal cemeteries;
2. Cremation facilities;
3. Enshrinement facilities.
(2) Where rights change as a result of the vesting of public facilities or other property pursuant to Article 32 of the Act, the project implementer shall request registration without delay after notifying the managing authority of the completion of the project.

Article 36 (Support for Village Infrastructure Development Costs)
The detailed criteria for support for village infrastructure development costs under Article 34 of the Act shall be the criteria in subparagraph 2 of attached Table 1 of the Regulations on Standards for Bearing Expenses for Natural Disaster Relief and Recovery. <Amended 2012.4.10, 2016.11.1>

Article 37 Deleted. <2020.3.3>

